{title: God is great in my soul}
{subtitle: Hymnal 297}

{comment: Chorus}
God is great and greatly to be praised, God is great in my soul
God is great and greatly to be praised, God is great in my soul

{comment: Verse 1}
God’s greatness is seen, In the Heavens above,
In the world He established on the floods.
The glory of His greatness seen on Calvary,
Where He shed His precious blood.

{comment: Verse 2}
When Jesus He died The veil was rent in twain,
That separated man from God.
But now by faith we have access to Him,
All through His precious blood.

{comment: Verse 3}
He’s King of kings and Lord of lords,
My God is great in my soul.
He’s Father, Son, and Holy Ghost,
My God is great in my soul.
He’s balm of Gilead, the great physician,
My God is great in my soul,
Now by His stripes we’re healed of all disease,
My God is great in my soul.
